# Local-only docs (personal notes / already-distributed material).
# Most local-only docs live under docs/Local/ (concepts, analysis, From_Professor,
# Weekly_Progress_to_be_submitted, Plans/proposal.md, Plans/Xin_Implementation_Plan.md);
# the manual-review record keeps its own local-only set, listed further down.
# Everything else under docs/ IS tracked and shared with Teammate:
#   docs/Plans/ joint plan + scope + idea docs.
# Note: Xin's own completion logs are kept local-only (docs/Completion_Log/Xin_*);
#   the folder itself stays shared (README.md) for teammates' own logs.
docs/Local/
docs/Completion_Log/Xin_*
docs/specs/*.zh.md

# Working documents of the manual-review v1 record. These are the author's own
# in-progress material rather than part of the published record, so they are kept
# locally and are not committed.
#
#   per_case_analysis/  the 19 per-unit dossiers and their index.
#   taxonomy_todo.md    the full 26-section process specification, which this
#                       compressed path did not run.
#   tools/              the analysis tooling. It is one coupled unit that only
#                       runs against the working record and the workspace's own
#                       layout -- units.py imports recount.py, and check_landing.py
#                       and make_tables.py are written against those documents --
#                       so it cannot be committed piecemeal. It was already
#                       described in docs/manual_review_v1/README.md as
#                       provenance rather than an entry point.
#   references/2026-08-05-parallel-failure-taxonomy-review-pipeline-design.md
#                       a working pipeline design note.
#
# docs/manual_review_v1/README.md documents this exclusion for readers, and the
# repository's own entry point for labels and counts remains
# scripts/reporting/manual_review_category_counts.py, which needs none of these.
docs/manual_review_v1/per_case_analysis/
docs/manual_review_v1/taxonomy_todo.md
docs/manual_review_v1/tools/
docs/manual_review_v1/references/2026-08-05-parallel-failure-taxonomy-review-pipeline-design.md

# Failure-review run directories (large intermediate products: details.jsonl
# carries full paragraph text, plus generated failures_review.html). Code
# version is already traceable via config.json's git_commit, so runs are not
# committed. The formal results/dense_results.csv stays tracked.
results/runs/

# Per-reviewer manual-review case files. These embed the full top-50 paragraph
# text for every assigned unit, which is ~90% of their bytes and ~1.2 MB total.
# The review protocol makes Git retention optional ("ordinary file exchange is
# sufficient for review"), and these are the delivery artifacts handed to the
# other reviewer directly, so they are not committed. The shared page and the
# small assignment table in the same directory DO stay tracked, and both case
# files regenerate byte-for-byte from the read-only run via
# scripts/build_manual_review_batch.py.
results/annotations/*/*_cases.json
results/annotations/*/*_notes*.csv

